On Thu, 28 Jan 2010, G-Mon wrote:
> Careful with teleporting boulders, though; it does bad things to your
> luck

Actually, it doesn't.  I believe this is explicitly so because Sokoban
boulder teleport is already a Hail Mary.  The RNG can easily choose a new
location for the boulder that is even worse and not in range of a further
zap.

For example, if you zap a boulder because it is locked and you need it to
fill a hole, it will probably wind up in the room with the up stairs.

> (as does a bunch of boulder-related actions in Sokoban that don't
> involve pushing them).

But pretty much everything else IS indeed covered.  About the only
unpunished violation of Sokoban rules I can think of, is deliberately
falling into a hole so as to return to the entrance stair of a level, when
walking back would be impossible without locking a boulder.  I often used
this on the harder variant of the second floor.

